# Screens and widgets

`features/<feature>/screen/` holds the route widget only: layout and wiring. Canvas, toolbar, palette, and dialogs go in `features/<feature>/widgets/`, one widget per file.

A widget used by a second feature moves to `core/ui/widgets/`. Do not copy it.

Screens import `state/<its feature>/`, own `widgets/`, `core/ui/`, and `data/models`. They never import `data/api`, `data/local`, `core/storage`, or repository impls.

No brush geometry, clipping, or hit-testing in a widget. The widget paints; `core/engine` computes.

```dart
// BAD — clipping inside the canvas widget
class DrawingCanvas extends StatelessWidget {
  Widget build(context) { /* region path math here */ }
}

// GOOD — widget paints, engine clips
class DrawingCanvas extends StatelessWidget {
  Widget build(context) => CustomPaint(painter: LayerPainter(engine));
}
```
